{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2119-11-22 15:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hello, I'm Dr. Lee. I understand your physical therapist noticed a slow heart rate today. How are you feeling?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2119-11-22 15:16:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Hi, yes, my heart rate was in the 40s. I’ve had that before. I just feel a bit lightheaded, but that’s been going on for a while."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2119-11-22 15:17:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Okay, thanks. You don’t have chest pain, dizziness that comes and goes, or shortness of breath beyond your usual?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2119-11-22 15:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No chest pain. I do get short of breath walking, but that’s normal for me. The lightheadedness is more like a constant spinning."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2119-11-22 15:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Got it. We’ll monitor your heart rhythm and run some tests to make sure this isn’t dangerous. We’ve already done an EKG."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2119-11-22 15:20:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is it my heart medicine? I stopped my blood pressure pills because they made me too slow."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2119-11-22 15:21:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We reviewed your meds. You’re not on anything now that should cause severe bradycardia. We also checked your thyroid—your levels are normal."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2119-11-22 15:22:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. I just started gabapentin for neck pain—could that do it?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2119-11-22 15:23:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Gabapentin doesn’t typically slow the heart. We think your slow rate is likely due to your heart’s natural rhythm, especially with your history of heart disease."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2119-11-22 17:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your chest X-ray came back normal—no signs of heart failure or lung issues. That’s reassuring."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2119-11-22 17:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s good. I’ve had breathing trouble before, but it’s usually from my COPD."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2119-11-22 17:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. We’re continuing your inhalers. Your oxygen levels are stable, especially with a little supplemental oxygen."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2119-11-23 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your heart was monitored overnight. You stayed in sinus bradycardia, but no dangerous rhythms. Your troponin levels were negative—no heart attack."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2119-11-23 08:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So it’s not an emergency? I’ve had this rate before."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2119-11-23 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s right. Since you’re not having new symptoms and your tests are clear, we don’t think this episode is dangerous. Your dizziness seems more related to prior issues, not the slow rate."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2119-11-23 10:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re planning to discharge you soon. Keep taking your prescribed meds, especially acamprosate and thiamine—important since you’ve stopped drinking."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2119-11-23 10:16:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I haven’t had a drink in over a month. I know I need to stay away from alcohol."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2119-11-23 10:17:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s excellent. Also, keep using your inhalers regularly, even if you don’t always feel short of breath."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2119-11-23 10:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I forget sometimes. But I’ll try."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2119-11-23 10:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "And if you ever have chest pain, pass out, or your breathing gets worse, go to the ER right away."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2119-11-23 10:20:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "What about the dizziness?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2119-11-23 10:21:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Follow up with your primary doctor. It may be related to your previous stroke or inner ear issues, not your heart rate."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2119-11-23 11:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your discharge papers are ready. You’re going home with services to help with follow-up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2119-11-23 11:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, thanks. I’ll keep my appointments."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2119-11-23 11:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "One last thing—your levothyroxine dose was recently increased. Keep taking it daily and get your levels checked as scheduled."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2119-11-23 11:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve been taking it every morning. My energy’s a bit better."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2119-11-23 11:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Great. You’re doing the right things. We’ll see you in follow-up, but call sooner if anything changes."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2119-11-23 11:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you, Doctor."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2119-11-22 15:10:00",
    "admission_end": "2119-11-23 14:30:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A man with a history of CAD s/p CABG, COPD, chronic diastolic heart failure, hypothyroidism, and alcohol abuse was admitted after his physical therapist noted bradycardia with a heart rate in the 40s. He reported chronic lightheadedness but denied new symptoms such as chest pain, syncope, or worsening dyspnea. Evaluation included telemetry, EKG showing sinus bradycardia, normal cardiac enzymes, and a chest X-ray without acute findings. Thyroid function was normal, and no medication adjustments were made. His bradycardia was deemed asymptomatic and not requiring intervention. He remained stable, continued on his outpatient medications including acamprosate and thiamine, and was discharged home with services and follow-up instructions for dizziness and cardiac care.",
    "problems": [
      "Other specified cardiac dysrhythmias",
      "Chronic diastolic heart failure",
      "Congestive heart failure, unspecified",
      "Chronic airway obstruction, not elsewhere classified",
      "Coronary atherosclerosis of unspecified type of vessel, native or graft",
      "Unspecified essential hypertension",
      "Old myocardial infarction",
      "Other and unspecified hyperlipidemia",
      "Anemia, unspecified",
      "Aortocoronary bypass status"
    ]
  }
}
